---
// Sprachweiche der Wurzel.
//
// Vorher stand hier ein blankes <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url=/de/">.
// Damit landete JEDER Besucher auf Deutsch, auch der, dessen Browser kein Wort
// Deutsch anmeldet, und erfuhr von der englischen Fassung nur, wenn er den
// Umschalter im Kopf der Seite fand. GitHub Pages kann Accept-Language nicht
// auswerten, also entscheidet der Browser selbst, bevor irgendetwas gerendert
// wird.
//
// Regel: navigator.languages wird in seiner REIHENFOLGE durchlaufen, und es
// gewinnt der erste Eintrag, der eine der beiden angebotenen Sprachen bezeichnet.
// Zuvor stand hier ein some() auf "de", das ["en-GB","en","de-DE"] nach /de/
// schickte, obwohl Englisch die erste Wahl ist: in Deutschland der Regelfall bei
// Zugezogenen und bei internationalen Vermittlern. Nennt die Liste keine der
// beiden Sprachen, bleibt es bei /de/. location.replace statt href, damit der
// Zurück-Knopf den Besucher nicht in diese Seite zurückwirft.
//
// Ohne JavaScript passiert nichts, und das ist die Absicht: die beiden sichtbaren
// Links im Body sind der Rückfall. Das <noscript> mit Sofortweiterleitung, das
// hier stand, schickte ausgerechnet diese Besucher wieder alle nach /de/.
---
<html lang="de">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Michael Boiman</title>
  {/* This page is its own destination, not a copy of the German one: it is the
      only page that lets a visitor choose, which is exactly what x-default
      names. Canonical points here for the same reason. It carried
      robots="noindex,follow" and a canonical to /de/ for a while, which told a
      crawler that the one page offering both languages does not exist; the root
      is already excluded from the sitemap (see astro.config.mjs), so nothing
      needed the noindex. */}
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://mboiman.github.io/" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="de" href="https://mboiman.github.io/de/" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://mboiman.github.io/en/" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://mboiman.github.io/" />
  <script is:inline>
    // Same storage key and the same two values the toggle in
    // src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro writes, so a visitor who picked light on the
    // CV page does not get a dark flash on the way in. With nothing stored, the
    // media query in the style block decides, which is now also what `system`
    // means: the key is ABSENT in that state, so there is nothing to read here
    // and the media query is the whole answer.
    //
    // The key was renamed with the three state control. This page is the reason
    // to say so out loud: it is the second reader of that key and it lives
    // outside the layout, so a rename that only touched BaseLayout would have
    // left the root page silently reading a name nobody writes any more. It
    // would not have failed anything, it would just have stopped matching.
    (() => {
      try {
        const saved = localStorage.getItem('theme-choice');
        if (saved === 'dark' || saved === 'light') {
          document.documentElement.classList.add(saved);
        }
      } catch {}
    })();
  </script>
  <script is:inline>
    // Priority order, not "does the list contain de somewhere".
    (() => {
      const offered = ['de', 'en'];
      try {
        const tags = (navigator.languages && navigator.languages.length
          ? navigator.languages
          : [navigator.language]).filter(Boolean);
        let target = '';
        for (const tag of tags) {
          const base = String(tag).toLowerCase().split('-')[0];
          if (offered.indexOf(base) !== -1) { target = base; break; }
        }
        location.replace('/' + (target || 'de') + '/');
      } catch {
        location.replace('/de/');
      }
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    /* Copies of the tokens in src/styles/global.css, read from there on
       2026-08-22 (:root and html.dark). This page cannot import the stylesheet:
       it has to paint before it redirects, from one file. Copying the values
       raw is what went wrong before, so they sit in variables under the token
       names they came from, and a divergence is one grep away. Two of the five
       were wrong: the link used --accent-hover (#1d4ed8) rather than --accent,
       and the dark text used #e2e8f0 where --text is #f8fbff. */
    :root {
      --bg: #f8fbff;
      --text: #17212b;
      --accent: #2563eb;
    }
    /* A stored light choice beats the system setting, which is why the media
       rule steps aside for .light. Only the two explicit choices set a class;
       "follow the system" sets none. */
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root:not(.light) {
        --bg: #0f172a;
        --text: #f8fbff;
        --accent: #93c5fd;
      }
    }
    :root.dark {
      --bg: #0f172a;
      --text: #f8fbff;
      --accent: #93c5fd;
    }
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; min-height: 100vh;
           display: grid; place-items: center;
           background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); }
    ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; font-size: 1rem; }
    a { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <nav aria-label="Sprache wählen">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/de/" hreflang="de">Zur deutschen Fassung</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/" hreflang="en" lang="en">Go to the English version</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</body>
</html>
